                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Scaevola: [[Hype game]] [honest] Mechanicus(game) +fun +intelligent +omnissiah_approved +easily_understood +pleasantly_complex [[[witheld 36 praise arguments: briefness is imperative]]] // MUST_BUY == TRUE \r\n\r\nRho: Finantial cost of game is lesser than the value of experiencing it. Acquisition of media is justifiable and beneficial.\r\n\r\nKhepra: This game will substantially raise your morale. I do not like spending my credits, but this is a worthy sacrifice.\r\n\r\nVidex: This videogame encapsulates the righteousness of the Mechanicus in such brilliance that it might as well be considered sacred scripture. [i]Lessons in Perfection[/i], verse 84, \"beautiful is that which witholds nothing in exalting the Omnissiah.\"\r\n\r\nCaprix: It would be folly not to buy this game. Prices on sales are overwhelmingly advantageous. Wait for a sale, but waste no time in buying once it arrives.\r\n\r\nTiresus: I have made most fascinating discoveries about the different necron lifeforms that exist. Knowledge of them prior to this game was superficial. I now wish for more samples of lore.\r\n\r\nFaustinius: My emotional cores return amusement from the gameplay, and beauty from its soundtrack. I see no reason not to get it, and all the reason for liking it.",
